{{! How the routes of activities are drawn, as JSON (the page reads it).  Routes are thin red threads, each moved a little
    to the side of its direction of travel by an amount of its own (spread_m, in metres), so that routes over the same
    road look like one line from far and like several threads from close.  The climbs are placed beside the threads, using
    spread_m.  A colour can be a tag for one of the terminal's colours (red, green, blue, yellow, grey, as in the line
    below) or any #rrggbb. }}
{
  "routes": { "color": "{{{red}}}", "weight": 3, "opacity": 0.85, "spread_m": 4 }
}
